      "notesInFlow": true,
      "notes": "The Convert to File node serves as the final structural bridge in a data pipeline, taking structured JavaScript Object Notation (JSON) items and packing them into standard flat-file formats like CSV or Excel. In the context of your workflow, this node compiles the merged student stream into a single downloadable artifact. However, its placement immediately following the Merge node dictates a specific downstream behavior: because the Merge node re-combines all records into a unified array, the Convert to File node outputs one comprehensive master file rather than segregated lists. If your objective shifts toward archiving separate records by location or email health, this single compilation node must be replaced by individual file generation nodes on each isolated branch"
